# Python API standards

Stack: FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2, Alembic, Pydantic, PostgreSQL. Python 3.12+.

## Layout per domain module (`apps/api/src/homehub/modules/<domain>/`)

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `router.py` | FastAPI routes only — deps, call service, map to response |
| `service.py` | Use cases; raise domain exceptions |
| `repository.py` | DB access for this module’s tables |
| `schemas.py` | Pydantic request/response models |
| `models.py` | SQLAlchemy ORM models |
| `exceptions.py` | Module-specific `HomeHubError` subclasses |

Do not query another module’s ORM models from your repository — call that module’s service.

## Async

- Prefer `async def` routes and `async` DB if using async driver; be consistent within the app.
- No blocking I/O on the event loop (use thread pool or sync worker for CPU-heavy work).
- Background work: `apps/api/src/homehub/jobs/`, not fire-and-forget in routes without a queue.

## Errors

- Services raise typed exceptions; router maps to HTTP status via centralized handlers in `main.py` or `middleware/errors.py`.
- Validate input with Pydantic at the boundary only.

## Tenancy and auth

- Every family-scoped service method receives `family_id` and `current_user` (or equivalent) from router deps.
- Assert membership/role before read or write.

## Formatting and types

- Ruff for lint + format (line length per `pyproject.toml` when present).
- Type hints on all public service and repository functions.

## Tests

- Unit: `apps/api/tests/unit/` mirroring module path.
- Integration: `apps/api/tests/integration/` with real PostgreSQL (container or compose).
- Name files `test_<module>.py`; functions `test_<behavior>`.
